+# Train 35 hosted test portability
+
+Audit: `/tmp/sol35-ci-audit.md`, Train 35 SHA `fa4a5f2e785c73e32216931e33cdbe140c06647d`, run `43786984969`. This is a source-only repair; the concurrent build worker owns generated build files.
+
+## Repairs
+
+- `tests/src/gui/TouchLayoutTest.cpp`: qualify `viewOf`'s return type, range variable and `findChildren` template type, plus both local view declarations. This covers the MSVC C2872 ambiguity between `lmms::ClipView` and `lmms::gui::ClipView` (audit log line 5102 and follow-ons 5111/5113). Existing touch assertions remain unchanged.
+- `tests/src/core/RemotePluginAudioPortsTest.cpp`: guard `g_criticalsSeen` and `countCriticals` with `SYNC_WITH_SHM_FIFO`, matching their two guarded users at source lines 1284 and 1340. Both critical-message assertions remain.
+- `tests/src/gui/MixerSendsOnFadersTest.cpp`: create the expected volume list with a count-bounded append loop, preserving count and order without relying on the removed Qt list repeat constructor. Existing comparisons remain.
+- `tests/train-51-portability-check.py`: extend the registered Train 51 checker. The touch probe compiles the extracted real helper and actual declarations with both `lmms::ClipView` and `lmms::gui::ClipView` visible; separate negative controls unqualify the real helper use and `lowerView`. The remote probe compiles the extracted guarded definitions in an anonymous namespace with `-c -o` and requires `countCriticals` plus `unused-function` in the red diagnostic. The list probe compiles the fixed source expression and the original repeat expression with Qt 5 headers; Qt 6 green is optional when installed. Existing RowTableView Qt 5/optional Qt 6, MIDI unused-function and SFZ missing-API controls remain.
+
+## Targets
+
+Audit jobs covered: `msvc-x64` (TouchLayoutTest); `mingw64` (RemotePluginAudioPortsTest); `linux-arm64`, `macos-x86_64`, `linux-x86_64`, `windows-arm64`, and `macos-arm64` (MixerSendsOnFadersTest). The audit's Windows ARM stdin warning was not a source failure. Four earlier Train 51 fixes and all their assertions remain untouched.
